IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Part IV, continued: ss 40 to 43 (exercise of powers and duties, appointments, delegations, distances).
-- Where a function says "the section provides", JUST TRUE means the section gives the consequence in the case and JUST FALSE means it does not
-- (its condition fails, or the contrary intention appears); NOTHING means the case is outside what the section addresses.

§ `Part IV -- Provisions applicable to Acts and subordinate instruments (continued)`

§§ `s 40 Exercise of powers and performance of duties`

-- s 40(a): unless the contrary intention appears, where an Act or subordinate instrument confers a power or imposes a duty, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
-- src:918 | (a) from time to time as occasion requires; and
@ref s 40(a) (src:918)
GIVEN anActOrInstrumentConfersAPowerOrImposesADuty IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s40(a) the power may be exercised and the duty performed from time to time as occasion requires` MEANS
    IF anActOrInstrumentConfersAPowerOrImposesADuty AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE VicPersonRelativeToAnOffice IS ONE OF
    VicThePersonForTheTimeBeingHoldingTheOffice
    VicThePersonForTheTimeBeingActingInTheOffice
    VicThePersonForTheTimeBeingPerformingTheDutiesOfTheOffice
    VicSomeoneElse

-- s 40(b): if the power or duty is conferred or imposed on the holder of an office or position as such, it is exercised or performed by the person for the time being holding, acting in or performing the duties of the office or position.
-- src:919 | (b) if conferred or imposed on the holder of an office or position as such, by the person for the time being holding, acting in or performing the duties of the office or position.
@ref s 40(b) (src:919)
GIVEN conferredOrImposedOnTheHolderOfAnOfficeOrPositionAsSuch IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, person IS A VicPersonRelativeToAnOffice
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s40(b) the person is the one by whom the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT conferredOrImposedOnTheHolderOfAnOfficeOrPositionAsSuch THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF person EQUALS VicSomeoneElse THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 41 Power to appoint`

DECLARE VicIncidentalPowerOfAnAppointer IS ONE OF
    VicAppointAPersonToActUntilAPersonIsAppointedToTheOffice                  -- s 41(1)(a)(i)
    VicAppointAPersonToActDuringAVacancyInTheOffice                           -- s 41(1)(a)(ii)
    VicRemoveAPersonAppointedToTheOffice                                      -- s 41(1)(b)
    VicSuspendAPersonAppointedAndAppointAnotherTemporarilyInTheirPlace        -- s 41(1)(c)
    VicAppointAPersonToActInPlaceOfAnAbsentOrUnableHolder                     -- s 41(1)(d)
    VicAppointAPersonToPerformAParticularFunctionOnAParticularOccasion        -- s 41(1)(e)
    VicAnyOtherPowerRelatedToTheAppointment

-- s 41(1): if an Act or subordinate instrument confers on a person or body (the appointer) a power to appoint a person to an office, the power, unless the contrary intention appears, includes the powers in paragraphs (a) to (e).
-- Paragraph (d) applies if the holder is absent or, for any other reason, unable to perform the functions and duties of the office; paragraph (e) if the holder is unable to perform a particular function or duty on a particular occasion.
-- src:923 | (1) If an Act or subordinate instrument confers on a person or body (the appointer) a power to appoint a person to an office, the power, unless the contrary intention appears, includes a power—
-- src:925 | (a) to appoint a person to act in the office—
-- src:927 | (i) until a person is appointed to the office; or
-- src:928 | (ii) during a vacancy in the office;
-- src:929 | (b) to remove a person appointed to the office;
-- src:930 | (c) to suspend a person appointed to the office and to appoint another person temporarily in the place of the person so suspended;
-- src:931 | (d) if the holder of the office is absent or, for any other reason, unable to perform the functions and duties of the office, to appoint a person to act in place of the holder;
-- src:932 | (e) if the holder of the office is, for any reason, unable to perform a particular function or duty on a particular occasion or in relation to a particular matter, to appoint a person to perform that function or duty on that occasion or in relation to that matter.
@ref s 41(1) (src:923-932)
GIVEN conferredAPowerToAppointAPersonToAnOffice IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, power IS A VicIncidentalPowerOfAnAppointer, holderIsAbsentOrUnableToPerformTheFunctionsAndDuties IS A BOOLEAN, holderIsUnableToPerformAParticularFunctionOnAParticularOccasion IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s41(1) the power to appoint includes the power` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT conferredAPowerToAppointAPersonToAnOffice THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF power EQUALS VicAnyOtherPowerRelatedToTheAppointment THEN NOTHING
        IF power EQUALS VicAppointAPersonToActInPlaceOfAnAbsentOrUnableHolder AND (NOT holderIsAbsentOrUnableToPerformTheFunctionsAndDuties) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF power EQUALS VicAppointAPersonToPerformAParticularFunctionOnAParticularOccasion AND (NOT holderIsUnableToPerformAParticularFunctionOnAParticularOccasion) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE VicKindOfAppointmentMadeUnderS41 IS ONE OF
    VicAppointmentToActInTheOffice                                       -- s 41(1)(a), (c) or (d)
    VicAppointmentToPerformAFunctionOnAParticularOccasion                -- s 41(1)(e)
    VicAppointmentNotMadeUnderSubsection1

DECLARE VicIncidentOfAnAppointmentUnderS41 IS ONE OF
    VicAppointerMayDetermineTheTermsAndConditionsIncludingRemunerationAndAllowances   -- s 41(2)(a)(i)
    VicAppointerMayTerminateTheAppointmentAtAnyTime                                   -- s 41(2)(a)(ii)
    VicAppointmentCeasesToHaveEffectOnTheAppointeesResignationInWritingDeliveredToTheAppointer   -- s 41(2)(b)
    VicAppointeeHasAndMayExerciseAllThePowersAndPerformsAllTheFunctionsAndDutiesOfTheHolder   -- s 41(2)(c)(i)
    VicAppointeeHasAndMayExerciseAllThePowersNecessaryForPerformingThatFunctionOrDuty         -- s 41(2)(d)(i)
    VicTheActAppliesInRelationToTheAppointmentAsIfTheAppointeeWereTheHolder                   -- s 41(2)(c)(ii) and (d)(ii)

-- s 41(2): the paragraphs apply in relation to an appointment made under subsection (1).
-- (a) the appointer may fix the terms and conditions and may terminate at any time; (b) the appointment ceases on written resignation delivered to the appointer;
-- (c) while the appointee is acting in the office under subsection (1) (except paragraph (e)), subject to the terms and conditions, the appointee has all the powers and functions and this or any other Act applies as if the appointee were the holder;
-- (d) while the appointee is appointed to perform a function or duty on a particular occasion, subject to the terms and conditions, the appointee has the powers necessary for performing it and this or any other Act applies as if the appointee were the holder.
-- The input conditionOfTheIncidentHolds is the fact the paragraph names: the resignation was in writing and delivered to the appointer (b), or the appointee is for the time being acting (c) or appointed for the occasion (d).
-- src:933 | (2) The following paragraphs apply in relation to an appointment of a person (the appointee) made under subsection (1)—
-- src:934 | (a) the appointer—
-- src:935 | (i) may determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances (if any);
-- src:936 | (ii) may terminate the appointment at any time;
-- src:937 | (b) the appointment ceases to have effect if the appointee resigns in writing delivered to the appointer;
-- src:938 | (c) while the appointee is acting in the office under subsection (1) (except paragraph (e)), then, subject to the terms and conditions of the appointment—
-- src:939 | (i) the appointee has and may exercise all the powers, and shall perform all the functions and duties, of the holder of the office; and
-- src:940 | (ii) this or any other Act applies in relation to the appointment as if the appointee were the holder of the office;
-- src:941 | (d) while the appointee is appointed to perform a function or duty on a particular occasion or in relation to a particular matter, then, subject to the terms and conditions of the appointment—
-- src:942 | (i) the appointee has and may exercise all the powers of the holder of the office necessary for performing that function or duty; and
-- src:943 | (ii) this or any other Act applies in relation to the appointment as if the appointee were the holder of the office.
@ref s 41(2) (src:933-943)
GIVEN kind IS A VicKindOfAppointmentMadeUnderS41, incident IS A VicIncidentOfAnAppointmentUnderS41, conditionOfTheIncidentHolds IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s41(2) the incident follows from the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS VicAppointmentNotMadeUnderSubsection1 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointerMayDetermineTheTermsAndConditionsIncludingRemunerationAndAllowances THEN JUST TRUE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointerMayTerminateTheAppointmentAtAnyTime THEN JUST TRUE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointeeHasAndMayExerciseAllThePowersAndPerformsAllTheFunctionsAndDutiesOfTheHolder THEN JUST (kind EQUALS VicAppointmentToActInTheOffice AND conditionOfTheIncidentHolds)
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointeeHasAndMayExerciseAllThePowersNecessaryForPerformingThatFunctionOrDuty THEN JUST (kind EQUALS VicAppointmentToPerformAFunctionOnAParticularOccasion AND conditionOfTheIncidentHolds)
        OTHERWISE JUST conditionOfTheIncidentHolds

-- s 41(3): if the power to make an appointment to an office is exercisable only on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of some other person or body,
-- the power to make an appointment to act in the office, or to remove or suspend, is only exercisable on that recommendation, or subject to that approval or consent, unless the contrary intention appears.
-- src:944 | (3) If the power of a person or body to make an appointment to an office is exercisable only on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of some other person or body, the power to make an appointment to act in the office, or to remove or suspend, is only exercisable on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of that other person or body, unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 41(3) (src:944)
GIVEN theAppointmentPowerIsExercisableOnlyOnTheRecommendationOrApprovalOrConsentOfAnother IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, power IS A VicIncidentalPowerOfAnAppointer
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s41(3) the power is only exercisable on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of that other person or body` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT theAppointmentPowerIsExercisableOnlyOnTheRecommendationOrApprovalOrConsentOfAnother THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF power EQUALS VicAppointAPersonToPerformAParticularFunctionOnAParticularOccasion THEN NOTHING
        IF power EQUALS VicAnyOtherPowerRelatedToTheAppointment THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 41AA Acting appointments`

DECLARE VicIncidentOfAnActingAppointment IS ONE OF
    VicAppointmentMayBeExpressedToHaveEffectOnlyInSpecifiedCircumstances            -- s 41AA(a)
    VicAppointerMayDetermineTheTermsAndConditions                                   -- s 41AA(b)(i)
    VicActingAppointerMayTerminateTheAppointmentAtAnyTime                                 -- s 41AA(b)(ii)
    VicAppointeeMayContinueToActWhileTheOfficeIsVacantUntilDirectedOrAppointed      -- s 41AA(c)
    VicAppointmentCeasesOnWrittenResignationDeliveredToTheAppointer                 -- s 41AA(e)
    VicAppointeeHasAllThePowersFunctionsAndDutiesOfTheHolder                        -- s 41AA(f)(i)(A)
    VicAppointeeHasThePowersNecessaryForTheParticularFunctionOrDuty                 -- s 41AA(f)(i)(B)
    VicTheActAppliesAsIfTheAppointeeWereTheHolder                                   -- s 41AA(f)(ii)

-- s 41AA: if a provision of an Act (other than s 41) or of a subordinate instrument confers a power to appoint a person to act in a particular office, then, except so far as the Act or subordinate instrument otherwise provides, paragraphs (a) to (f) follow.
-- The input conditionOfTheIncidentHolds is the fact the paragraph names: the office is or becomes vacant while the appointee is acting (c), the resignation is in writing and delivered to the appointer (e), the appointee is acting (f).
-- Paragraph (f)(i)(A) is the case of an appointment to act generally and (f)(i)(B) of an appointment made for the particular function or duty ("as the case requires").
-- src:948 | 41AA Acting appointments
-- src:949 | If a provision of an Act (other than section 41 of this Act) or of a subordinate instrument confers on a person or body (the appointer) a power to appoint a person (the appointee) to act in a particular office, then, except so far as the Act or subordinate instrument otherwise provides—
-- src:950 | (a) the appointment may be expressed to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment or in relation to a particular function or duty or on a particular occasion or in relation to a particular matter;
-- src:951 | (b) the appointer—
-- src:952 | (i) may determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances (if any);
-- src:953 | (ii) may terminate the appointment at any time;
-- src:954 | (c) if the office is, or becomes, vacant while the appointee is acting, the appointee may, subject to paragraph (a), continue to act until—
-- src:955 | (i) the appointer otherwise directs; or
-- src:956 | (ii) a person is appointed to the office or the vacancy is filled—
-- src:957 | whichever first occurs;
-- src:958 | (e) the appointment ceases to have effect if the appointee resigns in writing delivered to the appointer;
-- src:959 | (f) while the appointee is acting in the office, then, subject to the terms and conditions of the appointment—
-- src:960 | (i) the appointee has and may exercise—
-- src:961 | (A) all the powers, and shall perform all the functions and duties, of the holder of the office; or
-- src:962 | (B) all the powers of the holder of the office necessary for performing the particular function or duty for which the appointment is made—
-- src:963 | as the case requires; and
-- src:964 | (ii) this or any other Act applies in relation to the appointment as if the appointee were the holder of the office.
@ref s 41AA (src:948-964)
GIVEN conferredByAProvisionOtherThanSection41 IS A BOOLEAN, otherwiseProvided IS A BOOLEAN, incident IS A VicIncidentOfAnActingAppointment, conditionOfTheIncidentHolds IS A BOOLEAN, appointmentIsMadeForAParticularFunctionOrDuty IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s41AA the acting appointment has the incident` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT conferredByAProvisionOtherThanSection41 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF otherwiseProvided THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointeeHasAllThePowersFunctionsAndDutiesOfTheHolder AND appointmentIsMadeForAParticularFunctionOrDuty THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointeeHasThePowersNecessaryForTheParticularFunctionOrDuty AND (NOT appointmentIsMadeForAParticularFunctionOrDuty) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointeeMayContinueToActWhileTheOfficeIsVacantUntilDirectedOrAppointed AND (NOT conditionOfTheIncidentHolds) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointmentCeasesOnWrittenResignationDeliveredToTheAppointer AND (NOT conditionOfTheIncidentHolds) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointeeHasAllThePowersFunctionsAndDutiesOfTheHolder AND (NOT conditionOfTheIncidentHolds) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicAppointeeHasThePowersNecessaryForTheParticularFunctionOrDuty AND (NOT conditionOfTheIncidentHolds) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicTheActAppliesAsIfTheAppointeeWereTheHolder AND (NOT conditionOfTheIncidentHolds) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE VicWhoEndsTheContinuedActing IS ONE OF
    VicTheAppointerDirectsOtherwise
    VicAPersonIsAppointedToTheOfficeOrTheVacancyIsFilled
    VicBothHappenOnTheSameDay
    VicNeitherHasHappened

-- s 41AA(c): the appointee may continue to act until the appointer otherwise directs, or a person is appointed to the office or the vacancy is filled, whichever first occurs.
-- The days are those on which each event happens (NOTHING if it has not happened); the answer is the day the continued acting ends, and which event ended it.
-- src:954 | (c) if the office is, or becomes, vacant while the appointee is acting, the appointee may, subject to paragraph (a), continue to act until—
-- src:955 | (i) the appointer otherwise directs; or
-- src:956 | (ii) a person is appointed to the office or the vacancy is filled—
-- src:957 | whichever first occurs;
@ref s 41AA(c) (src:954-957)
GIVEN dayTheAppointerDirectsOtherwise IS A MAYBE DATE, dayAPersonIsAppointedOrTheVacancyIsFilled IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s41AA(c) the day on which the continued acting ends, whichever event first occurs` MEANS
    CONSIDER dayTheAppointerDirectsOtherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN dayAPersonIsAppointedOrTheVacancyIsFilled
    WHEN JUST directed THEN
        CONSIDER dayAPersonIsAppointedOrTheVacancyIsFilled
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST directed
        WHEN JUST filled THEN (IF directed LESS THAN filled THEN JUST directed ELSE JUST filled)

-- src:954 | (c) if the office is, or becomes, vacant while the appointee is acting, the appointee may, subject to paragraph (a), continue to act until—
-- src:955 | (i) the appointer otherwise directs; or
-- src:956 | (ii) a person is appointed to the office or the vacancy is filled—
-- src:957 | whichever first occurs;
@ref s 41AA(c) which event first occurs (src:954-957)
GIVEN dayTheAppointerDirectsOtherwise IS A MAYBE DATE, dayAPersonIsAppointedOrTheVacancyIsFilled IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A VicWhoEndsTheContinuedActing
`s41AA(c) which event ends the continued acting` MEANS
    CONSIDER dayTheAppointerDirectsOtherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER dayAPersonIsAppointedOrTheVacancyIsFilled
        WHEN NOTHING THEN VicNeitherHasHappened
        WHEN JUST filled THEN VicAPersonIsAppointedToTheOfficeOrTheVacancyIsFilled
    WHEN JUST directed THEN
        CONSIDER dayAPersonIsAppointedOrTheVacancyIsFilled
        WHEN NOTHING THEN VicTheAppointerDirectsOtherwise
        WHEN JUST filled THEN (IF filled LESS THAN directed THEN VicAPersonIsAppointedToTheOfficeOrTheVacancyIsFilled ELSE (IF directed LESS THAN filled THEN VicTheAppointerDirectsOtherwise ELSE VicBothHappenOnTheSameDay))

§§ `s 41A Power to make instrument includes power to revoke or amend`

-- s 41A: if an Act or subordinate instrument confers power to make, issue or grant an instrument (not being a subordinate instrument), the power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same conditions or limitations (if any), to repeal, revoke, rescind, amend, alter or vary an instrument made in the exercise of that power.
-- src:967 | 41A Power to make instrument includes power to revoke or amend
-- src:968 | If an Act or subordinate instrument confers power to make, issue or grant an instrument (not being a subordinate instrument) the power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same conditions or limitations (if any), to repeal, revoke, rescind, amend, alter or vary an instrument made in the exercise of that power.
@ref s 41A (src:967-968)
GIVEN conferredPowerToMakeIssueOrGrantAnInstrumentThatIsNotASubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s41A the power includes a power to repeal, revoke, rescind, amend, alter or vary an instrument made in the exercise of it` MEANS
    IF conferredPowerToMakeIssueOrGrantAnInstrumentThatIsNotASubordinateInstrument AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 42 Exercise of delegated powers`

-- s 42(1): where the discharge, exercise or performance of a responsibility, power, authority, duty or function is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person and is, in accordance with the Act or subordinate instrument, delegated,
-- the delegate may, unless the contrary intention appears, discharge, exercise or perform it upon the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind.
-- src:971 | (1) Where the discharge, exercise or performance by a person of a responsibility, power, authority, duty or function under an Act or subordinate instrument is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of that person in relation to a matter and the responsibility, power, authority, duty or function is, in accordance with the Act or subordinate instrument, delegated, the delegate may, unless the contrary intention appears, discharge, exercise or perform the responsibility, power, authority, duty or function upon the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind (as the case requires) in relation to that matter.
@ref s 42(1) (src:971)
GIVEN dependsUponTheOpinionBeliefOrStateOfMindOfThatPerson IS A BOOLEAN, delegatedInAccordanceWithTheActOrInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s42(1) the delegate may act upon the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind` MEANS
    IF dependsUponTheOpinionBeliefOrStateOfMindOfThatPerson AND delegatedInAccordanceWithTheActOrInstrument AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 42(2): subsection (1) applies to a delegation made under an Act or subordinate instrument whether made before or after the commencement of this Act.
-- src:972 | (2) Subsection (1) applies in relation to a delegation made under an Act or subordinate instrument, whether the delegation was made before or after the commencement of this Act.
@ref s 42(2) (src:972)
GIVEN madeUnderAnActOrSubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, dayTheDelegationWasMade IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s42(2) subsection (1) applies to the delegation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT madeUnderAnActOrSubordinateInstrument THEN NOTHING
        IF dayTheDelegationWasMade LESS THAN `s2 day the Act came into operation` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 42A Construction of power to delegate`

DECLARE VicIncidentOfAPowerToDelegate IS ONE OF
    VicTheExistingPowerToDelegateIncludesThePowerToDelegateThatPowerOfDelegation  -- s 42A(1)(aa) (the section provides it does NOT)
    VicTheDelegationPreventsTheDischargeByThePersonOrBody                          -- s 42A(1)(a) (the section provides it does NOT)
    VicTheDelegationMayBeMadeSubjectToConditionsOrLimitations                      -- s 42A(1)(b)
    VicTheDelegatedMatterWhenDischargedByTheDelegateIsTakenToBeDischargedByThePersonOrBody   -- s 42A(1)(c)

-- s 42A(1): if an Act or subordinate instrument confers on a person or body a power to delegate, then, unless the contrary intention appears,
-- (aa) the power to delegate does not include the power to delegate that power of delegation; (a) the delegation does not prevent the discharge by the person or body;
-- (b) the delegation may be made subject to conditions or limitations; (c) what is delegated, when discharged by the delegate, is taken to have been discharged by the person or body.
-- For (b) and (c) the answer is JUST TRUE where the section gives the proposition and JUST FALSE where its condition fails or the contrary intention appears.
-- For (aa) and (a) the section says the opposite ("does not include", "does not prevent"), so the proposition is JUST FALSE when the section applies and NOTHING when it does not (the text then says nothing about it).
-- src:976 | (1) If an Act or subordinate instrument confers on a person or body a power to delegate the discharge, exercise or performance of a responsibility, power, authority, duty or function under that or any other Act or subordinate instrument, then, unless the contrary intention appears—
-- src:978 | (aa) the power to delegate does not include the power to delegate that power of delegation;
-- src:979 | (a) the delegation does not prevent the discharge, exercise or performance of the responsibility, power, authority, duty or function by the person or body;
-- src:980 | (b) the delegation may be made subject to such conditions or limitations as the person or body may specify; and
-- src:981 | (c) a responsibility, power, authority, duty or function so delegated, when discharged, exercised or performed by the delegate, shall, for the purposes of the Act or subordinate instrument, be taken to have been discharged, exercised or performed by the person or body.
@ref s 42A(1) (src:976-981)
GIVEN conferredAPowerToDelegate IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, incident IS A VicIncidentOfAPowerToDelegate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s42A(1) the proposition about the delegation holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (incident EQUALS VicTheExistingPowerToDelegateIncludesThePowerToDelegateThatPowerOfDelegation OR incident EQUALS VicTheDelegationPreventsTheDischargeByThePersonOrBody) AND conferredAPowerToDelegate AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF incident EQUALS VicTheExistingPowerToDelegateIncludesThePowerToDelegateThatPowerOfDelegation OR incident EQUALS VicTheDelegationPreventsTheDischargeByThePersonOrBody THEN NOTHING
        IF conferredAPowerToDelegate AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 42A(2): if an Act or subordinate instrument confers power to delegate to the holder of an office or position, then, unless the contrary intention appears, a delegation may be made to any person for the time being acting in or performing the duties of that office or position.
-- src:982 | (2) If an Act or subordinate instrument confers power to delegate to the holder of an office or position, then, unless the contrary intention appears, a delegation may be made to any person for the time being acting in or performing the duties of that office or position.
@ref s 42A(2) (src:982)
GIVEN conferredPowerToDelegateToTheHolderOfAnOfficeOrPosition IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, personIsForTheTimeBeingActingInOrPerformingTheDutiesOfTheOffice IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s42A(2) a delegation may be made to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT conferredPowerToDelegateToTheHolderOfAnOfficeOrPosition THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF personIsForTheTimeBeingActingInOrPerformingTheDutiesOfTheOffice THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 42A(3) and (4): if a person or body delegates all (or one or more) of their responsibilities, powers, authorities, duties or functions and the Act or subordinate instrument is amended to confer additional ones (or to alter the scope of one),
-- then on and after the commencement of the amendment the delegation includes the additional ones (or the one as altered).
-- src:984 | (3) If—
-- src:985 | (a) a person or body delegates all of the person's or the body's responsibilities, powers, authorities, duties or functions under an Act or a subordinate instrument; and
-- src:986 | (b) that Act or subordinate instrument is amended to confer one or more additional responsibilities, powers, authorities, duties or functions—
-- src:987 | on and after the commencement of the amendment, the delegation includes the additional responsibilities, powers, authorities, duties or functions conferred by that amendment.
-- src:989 | (4) If—
-- src:990 | (a) a person or body delegates one or more of the person's or the body's responsibilities, powers, authorities, duties or functions under an Act or a subordinate instrument; and
-- src:991 | (b) that Act or subordinate instrument is amended to alter the scope of the responsibility, power, authority, duty or function—
-- src:992 | on and after the commencement of the amendment, the delegation includes the responsibility, power, authority, duty or function as altered by that amendment.
@ref s 42A(3) and s 42A(4) (src:984-992)
GIVEN delegatedAllOrOneOrMoreOfTheirFunctions IS A BOOLEAN, theActIsAmendedToConferAdditionalOrAlterTheScope IS A BOOLEAN, dayOfCommencementOfTheAmendment IS A DATE, dayOfQuestion IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s42A(3),(4) the delegation includes the additional or altered function on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (delegatedAllOrOneOrMoreOfTheirFunctions AND theActIsAmendedToConferAdditionalOrAlterTheScope) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF dayOfQuestion LESS THAN dayOfCommencementOfTheAmendment THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 42C Procedural defect or irregularity`

-- s 42C(1): a person's appointment to an office or position, and anything done by a person for the time being holding or acting in an office or position, is not ineffective only because of an irregularity in or in relation to the making of the person's appointment.
-- src:996 | (1) A person's appointment to an office or position, and anything done by a person for the time being holding or acting in an office or position, is not invalid only because of a defect or irregularity in or in relation to the making of the person's appointment to that office.
@ref s 42C(1) (src:996)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsAnIrregularityInTheMakingOfTheAppointment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s42C(1) the appointment, or what the person did, is ineffective because of the irregularity` MEANS
    IF theOnlyGroundIsAnIrregularityInTheMakingOfTheAppointment THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 42C(2): a delegation, and anything done under the delegation (including any subdelegation), is not ineffective only because of an irregularity in or in relation to the making of the delegation.
-- src:997 | (2) A delegation, and anything done under the delegation (including any subdelegation), is not invalid only because of a defect or irregularity in or in relation to the making of the delegation.
@ref s 42C(2) (src:997)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsAnIrregularityInTheMakingOfTheDelegation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s42C(2) the delegation, or what was done under it, is ineffective because of the irregularity` MEANS
    IF theOnlyGroundIsAnIrregularityInTheMakingOfTheDelegation THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 43 Measurement of distances`

-- s 43: in the measurement of a distance for the purposes of an Act or subordinate instrument, the distance shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
-- A straight line on a horizontal plane between two points ignores any difference in height: x and y are the position on that plane, and the distance is the length of the straight line between the two positions.
-- src:1001 | 43 Measurement of distances
-- src:1002 | In the measurement of a distance for the purposes of an Act or subordinate instrument, the distance shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref s 43 (src:1001-1002)
GIVEN firstX IS A NUMBER, firstY IS A NUMBER, secondX IS A NUMBER, secondY IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s43 length of the straight line on a horizontal plane between two positions` MEANS
    SQRT (((secondX MINUS firstX) TIMES (secondX MINUS firstX)) PLUS ((secondY MINUS firstY) TIMES (secondY MINUS firstY)))

-- src:1001 | 43 Measurement of distances
-- src:1002 | In the measurement of a distance for the purposes of an Act or subordinate instrument, the distance shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref s 43 (src:1001-1002)
GIVEN forTheMeasurementOfADistanceForAnActOrSubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s43 the distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` MEANS
    IF forTheMeasurementOfADistanceForAnActOrSubordinateInstrument AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
